nstead the fortune he would be facing  is overtaken by damage control headed up  by tony stark to tombs stark caused  destruction and now he's profiting from  it further shafting the little guy and  adding to his billions whilst adrian has  to live on the breadline there's an  amazing shot where we see stark tower  looming over central station and we pass  from that to tombs and his crew to see  them digging in the dirt on a symbolic  level it shows how stalk and people like  him tower above everything else whilst  the rest of us have to put our hands in  the mud to pick up their scraps the  introduction certainly tells us why  adrian is doing all this when he shows  us a drawing that his daughter is made  and though we don't know the pair are  related at this point it's easy to see  why he turns to a life of crime peter  later asks how he could do this still is  and tomb says that he's not doing it to  her he's doing it for her just before we  go to the title sequence tombs arrives  at his headquarters and says business is  good this is a very important line and  this intro basically has its own  self-contained arc in which we see a  supervillain origin for a working-class  man who was beaten by the elite turning  the situation on its side so that he can  win too it's important to bear in mind  not only for the car scene but also  peter's character too peter much like  tombs was only given things to do when  the elite needed him the airport scene  in civil war would have gone a lot worse  had he not been there but as soon as  that was over and stark no longer wanted  his help he was cast out to do things on  his own the majority of the first hour  of homecoming very much is peter  attempting to reach out to him and happy  but because they don't need him for  anything he's ghosted and told to stop  bothering them like tombs he's put in a  position where he has to do things on  his own because sticking to what they  say will simply have him stuck at being  the bottom rung of the ladder now peter  is idealistic and he desperately wants  to be an avenger therefore he attempts  to stop tombs whenever he can and a big  gut punch in the film comes when we  realize that he's actually the father of  liz aka peter's love interest there's a  couple of clues towards this in the  movie and for me it's up there with the  hydra twist in terms of how  unpredictable it was it leads to one of  the most tense scenes in the film in  which tombs figures out that peter  parker is spider-man  you guys hang out with spider-man  really  spider-man  wow  what's he like nice man  i've seen you around right baby i mean  somewhere we've uh have we ever because  of even the boys um he does accident to  kathleen with me  oh and it's at my party he disappeared  no no i did not disappear yes you did  you disappeared like you always do like  you did in dc too  that's terrible what happened down there  in dc though  were you  scared i bet you're glad and your old  pal spider-man showed up in the elevator  though  yo i i actually didn't go up i saw it  off on the ground  yeah very lucky that he was there that  day  good old spider-man  now this works for a number of reasons  tombs clearly recognizes peter but he  doesn't know where from he however  begins to piece it all together when  peter's absences become more and more  frequent he's left realizing that peter  parker is spider-man and john watts does  a brilliant turn with the lighting here  that shows exactly when the penny drops  tombs is that waiting at the red light  with it beaming across his face and then  this turns to green when adrian realizes  what's going on  good home spider-man  from here liz is dropped off and tomb  sits in the car with peter and he gives  him an ultimatum  nothing  more important than family you saved my  daughter's life  and i could never forget something like  that so i'm going to give you one chance  are you ready  you walk through those doors you forget  any of this happened  and don't you ever  ever  interfere with my business again  because if you do  i'll kill you  and everybody you love  hey  you just live your life  know what you say  thank you  you're welcome  now i'm gonna be completely honest with  you yeah there's been a couple of times  where i've watched this and i've  genuinely thought that if i was in that  position that i probably would have made  a partnership with tombs and we both  could have got rich together if i'd been  a high schooler yeah probably would have  just kept going out with liz made a  little business with her dad and sat  chilling ignoring the fact that my  spoiler sense was tingling i guess it's  lucky that i got bitten by a radioactive  attention seeker and decided to become a  youtuber as i would have sucked in this  role however peter and tombs are very  much parallels of one another and this  is why the latter gives the former a  choice tombs was in peter's position  once and he sees him as a naive teenager  who is simply trying to make their own  way in the world much like how he was in  fact when peter confronts tombs later on  he very much lays it out that people  like him are nothing to the elite peter  says that tomb selling weapons to people  is wrong and adrian reiterates the point  that that is exactly how stark made his  fortune he says that people like them  have to fight their wars and pick up  their scraps and because of this they  don't matter he is very much warning  peter of what will happen if he doesn't  get wise to the program and it's a very  chilling line juxtaposing this peter  sees tombs as his own future and what  will happen if he refuses to do the  right thing he's very much looking at  the older man that he could become if he  turns against what's true and though  tombs is living the high life it's truly  doomed to all come crashing down if  people like him stand up against it  tombs threatens to kill him and his  family if he interferes with his  business again and this clearly shakes  peter to the core most would walk away  and go to the dance and though it  initially seems like this is what peter  is going to do he still decides to take  tombs down even though it could have  massive repercussions due to his  identity being out there that's what  true heroes do and it's a defining  moment for the character that almost  kills him but in the end he becomes  stronger because of it now i know tony  often overshadows peter on the mcu but  this moment is very much a learning  experience for him too he very much  realizes that the people he's overlooked  are important and he ends up inviting  peter upstate because of the actions he  takes here however who this is most  important for is peter a person who up  until this point has been cast to the  side by the elite but because of his  moral fiber he hasn't taken a darker  path tombs did because he was weaker and  he ended up becoming the villain of the  story whereas peter who is given a  similar choice ends up becoming the hero  this is where the stakes are arguably  the highest for the character and even  though a big threat now knows his  identity he still puts his own needs to  the side in order to stop him it truly  is a defining moment for the character  and the way that the scene plays out is  absolutely perfect because we know that  peter could have easily lost and yet he  still charged ahead this is a spider-man  without his tech or allies taking  someone down because it's the right  thing to do it really defines not only  the character of the vulture but also  peter himself and why with great power  comes great responsibility peter could  easily use his gifts for his own  benefits but instead he applies them in  a way that will help the greater good  and because of this i think it's the  perfect spider-man scene it's one of my  favorite moments not only in the mcu but  in spider-man films in general and it's  something that i constantly go back to  as one of the best moments in well a  comic book movie ever  now obviously i'd love to hear your  thoughts on the scene so make sure you  comment below and let me know if you  think there's a better one with  spider-man that speaks more to you then  i'd love to hear it and as a thank you  for interacting with the video you'll be  put into a prize draw we are giving away  three mc box sets on the 30th of august  and all you have to do to be with the  chance of winning is like the video make  sure you subscribe with notifications on  and drop a comment below with your  thoughts on the moment we picked them at  random at the end of the month and the  winners of the last one are on screen  right now so if that's you then message  me on twitter at heavyspoilers if you  want something else to watch then make  sure you check out our breakdown of the  spiderman no way home trailer which will  be linked on screen right now we pointed  out all the easter eggs we could find  and also discussed how they call back to  the comics so it's definitely worth  checking out if you want to know more  without the way thank you for sending  through the video i've been paul i'll  see you next time take care peace

